"Let $E\\subseteq \\mathbb{R}/\\mathbb{Z}$ be an **Erdős semi-group (ESG)**, meaning a sub semi-group of $\\mathbb{R}/\\mathbb{Z}$, and suppose that $E$ has full Hausdorff dimension.\n\n**Full-dimension Erdős semi-group conjecture.** If $E$ is an ESG with full Hausdorff dimension, then\n\n$$\nE=\\mathbb{R}/\\mathbb{Z}.\n$$\n\nThe conjecture is presented as one of the paper's main motivations and is stated to imply Szemerédi's theorem on arithmetic progressions. The supplied text does not indicate whether it has been resolved."